    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Description\n\nHello, great set of plugins you've built!\r\n\r\nCurrently, mini.clue has a predefined behavior when pressing the \"special keys\". Those being `<Esc>`, `<C-c>`, `<CR>`, etc. I've found the default set of actions pretty logical, but it would be nice if the user could customize which keys do what actions. For example, I have `<Leader><CR>` mapped to `:nohl`, so instead of having the default `<CR>` execute a key query, it would be useful to remap that action to something like `<S-CR>` (or whatever the user determines to be better) instead, to avoid any conflicts with existing keymaps.\r\n\r\nI looked around in the documentation and code, and I didn't find an easy way to do this. If I'm mistaken please let me know.",
    "closed_at": "2023-10-20T11:00:07Z",
