    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for suggestion!\r\n\r\nYeah, currently `<Esc>`, `<C-c>`, `<CR>`, and `<BS>` have special meaning and can't be overridden. One of the main reasons is that there are very limited number of keys which are 1) intuitive for tasks they do; *and* 2) don't usually used as part of mapping; *and* 3) can be processed by `getcharstr()` powering key query process. For example, having `<S-CR>` and `<C-CR>` seems simply impossible (at least it depends on terminal emulator), while `<M-CR>` is possible.\r\n\r\nI am hesitant for adding too much customization to 'mini.nvim' modules. As 'mini.clue' already needs to be completely configured from ground up, I don't think this will happen. But I'll take time to think about it.",
